WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.780
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.513
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.813 --> 00:00:16.470
Unit eleven: Advanced Relative Clauses. Today you will build complex sentences with relative pronouns.

4
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.481
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:23.585
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.126
Whose.

7
00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:27.838
Whose means shows possession.

8
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.171
The man whose car broke down.

9
00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:33.006
Your turn. Say: Whose.

10
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:36.728
Whose.

11
00:00:37.483 --> 00:00:38.264
Where.

12
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.075
Where means used for places.

13
00:00:41.683 --> 00:00:43.033
The city where I live.

14
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:46.153
Your turn. Say: Where.

15
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:49.792
Where.

16
00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.191
When.

17
00:00:52.183 --> 00:00:53.951
When means used for times.

18
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:55.853
The day when we met.

19
00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.626
Your turn. Say: When.

20
00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:02.189
When.

21
00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.659
Reduced relative clause.

22
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:09.716
Reduced relative clause means a relative clause shortened with -ing or -ed.

23
00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:11.794
The man standing there.

24
00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:15.779
Your turn. Say: Reduced relative clause.

25
00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:20.703
Reduced relative clause.

26
00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.113
Preposition + which.

27
00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.766
Preposition + which means a formal pattern.

28
00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.932
The house in which I live.

29
00:01:29.517 --> 00:01:33.249
Your turn. Say: Preposition + which.

30
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.844
Preposition + which.

31
00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:40.362
Relative pronoun omission.

32
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:45.335
Relative pronoun omission means leaving out the pronoun when it is the object.

33
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.253
The book I read.

34
00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:51.129
Your turn. Say: Relative pronoun omission.

35
00:01:53.967 --> 00:01:55.955
Relative pronoun omission.

36
00:01:56.717 --> 00:01:58.031
Complex sentence.

37
00:01:59.017 --> 00:02:02.433
Complex sentence means a sentence with more than one clause.

38
00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:04.447
A complex sentence.

39
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:08.329
Your turn. Say: Complex sentence.

40
00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:12.888
Complex sentence.

41
00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.011
Subordinate clause.

42
00:02:16.017 --> 00:02:19.433
Subordinate clause means a clause that depends on the main clause.

43
00:02:20.017 --> 00:02:21.529
A subordinate clause.

44
00:02:22.117 --> 00:02:25.582
Your turn. Say: Subordinate clause.

45
00:02:28.433 --> 00:02:30.038
Subordinate clause.

46
00:02:30.833 --> 00:02:34.507
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:38.987
Visal, describe a place using where and a person using whose.

48
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:50.863
This is the city where I was born, and my neighbour, whose daughter is a doctor, lives next door. Where refers to places and whose to possession.

49
00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.217
How can we reduce a relative clause?

50
00:02:55.317 --> 00:03:05.039
We can use -ing or -ed: The man who is standing there becomes The man standing there. The books that were written by her becomes The books written by her.

51
00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.941
What about formal style?

52
00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:25.022
A preposition can come before which or whom: The house in which I live is old. When the relative pronoun is the object, we can omit it: The book I read was long. Never omit it when it is the subject.

53
00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:27.876
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:28.717 --> 00:03:32.794
Grammar focus: Advanced relative clauses: whose, where, when, reduced.

55
00:03:33.094 --> 00:03:34.409
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:35.117 --> 00:03:37.197
The city where I was born is small.

57
00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:40.013
The man standing there is my uncle.

58
00:03:40.917 --> 00:03:42.638
The house in which I live is old.

59
00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:53.885
Whose = possession; where = place; when = time. Reduce with -ing / -ed. After a preposition use which / whom. Omit the pronoun only if it is the object.

60
00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:58.696
Be careful! Don't say: The man who his car broke down.

61
00:04:00.633 --> 00:04:03.260
Say: The man whose car broke down.

62
00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.258
Use whose for possession.

63
00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:08.649
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:09.433 --> 00:04:11.119
Clauses Within Clauses.

65
00:04:11.419 --> 00:04:13.303
This is the town where I was born.

66
00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.101
My neighbour, whose daughter is a doctor, lives next door.

67
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.483
The man standing near the door is my uncle.

68
00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:24.859
The house in which I live was built in 1950.

69
00:04:25.867 --> 00:04:29.085
A subordinate clause adds detail to the main clause.

70
00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.724
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:37.862
The girl blank bag is blue is my cousin.

72
00:04:38.162 --> 00:04:41.687
A, who. B, which. C, whose.

73
00:04:45.233 --> 00:04:47.128
The answer is C: whose.

74
00:04:48.283 --> 00:04:50.480
The books blank by her are famous.

75
00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:53.725
A, wrote. B, written. C, writing.

76
00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:58.895
The answer is B: written.

77
00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.804
The year blank we met was 2018.

78
00:05:03.104 --> 00:05:06.270
A, when. B, where. C, whose.

79
00:05:09.833 --> 00:05:11.450
The answer is A: when.

80
00:05:12.583 --> 00:05:13.910
Which is more formal?

81
00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:19.558
A, the house in which I live. B, the house I live in. C, the house which I live.

82
00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.249
The answer is A: the house in which I live.

83
00:05:27.383 --> 00:05:30.614
According to the reading, what does the neighbour's daughter do?

84
00:05:30.914 --> 00:05:35.287
A, is a doctor. B, is a teacher. C, is a pilot.

85
00:05:38.833 --> 00:05:41.123
The answer is A: is a doctor.

86
00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:45.740
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:46.583 --> 00:05:49.488
Write a sentence using 'whose' in a relative clause.

88
00:05:58.283 --> 00:05:59.679
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:59.979 --> 00:06:10.750
I have a friend whose father owns a restaurant. It is the place where we celebrate every birthday. I use whose and where to combine two ideas in one sentence.

90
00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.363
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:20.258
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and advanced relative clauses: whose, where, when, reduced.

92
00:06:20.558 --> 00:06:25.741
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

93
00:06:26.041 --> 00:06:28.589
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

94
00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:31.704
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

